('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'IFRS 18: Presentation and Disclosure (Upcoming)','- **Effective Date**: January 1, 2027 (early adoption permitted).
- **Impact**: Replaces IAS 1. It introduces new defined categories in the statement of profit or loss (Operating, Investing, Financing) and requires disclosure of Management-defined Performance Measures (MPMs).','finance 01 Financial Reporting IFRS and Accounting','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting.md'),
('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'Sustainability Reporting (IFRS S1 & S2)','The research identifies UAE movement toward stronger sustainability and ESG disclosure practices, especially for listed entities and regulated reporting environments:
- **Listed-entity ESG disclosure**: Treat ESG reporting as a current governance and investor-reporting priority for listed entities, but verify the precise rule source, issuer category and filing format before reliance.
- **ISSB alignment**: IFRS S1 (General Requirements) and IFRS S2 (Climate-related Disclosures) are relevant global baseline standards for UAE sustainability-reporting development; the source materials do not establish a verified mandatory adoption date for all large private mainland entities.','finance 01 Financial Reporting IFRS and Accounting','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting.md'),
('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'5. Professional Practice and Certification','The accounting profession in the UAE is regulated by the **Accountants and Auditors Association (AAA)** and the **Ministry of Economy**.

- **UAECA (United Arab Emirates Chartered Accountant)**: The national qualification developed through a strategic partnership between the AAA and **ACCA**.
  > "A new national qualification has been implemented - the United Arab Emirates Chartered Accountant Qualification (UAECA)." — ACCA Global [[10]](#ref10)
- **Auditor Registration**: Practicing auditors must be registered with the Ministry of Economy and meet specific experience and residency requirements.
- **Ethics**: Professionals must adhere to the IESBA Code of Ethics, as adopted by the AAA.','finance 01 Financial Reporting IFRS and Accounting','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting.md'),
('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'6. Gaps and Verification Notes','- **IFRS 18 Local Guidance**: While IFRS 18 is issued globally, specific circulars from the SCA or CBUAE regarding local transition templates are expected closer to 2027.
- **Sustainability Deadlines**: The research does not provide a verified mandatory IFRS S1/S2 adoption date for large private mainland entities; treat the timing as **[verify before reliance]**.
- **Free Zone Variations**: While most free zones follow IFRS, some smaller/older free zones may have legacy reporting templates that require verification against the new Corporate Tax audit mandates.','finance 01 Financial Reporting IFRS and Accounting','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting.md'),
('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'IFRS 16 — Leases','Lease accounting affects UAE businesses with offices, retail units, warehouses, staff accommodation, vehicles, plant, and long-term right-of-use arrangements. A strong lease file contains the lease agreement, commencement date, non-cancellable period, renewal options, discount-rate support, payment schedule, modification log, and reconciliation to rent expense and right-of-use assets.','finance 01 Financial Reporting IFRS and Accounting','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting.md'),
('finance','01_Financial_Reporting_IFRS_and_Accounting',null,'Sources','- **UAE Ministry of Economy**: Federal Decree-Law No. 32 of 2021 on Commercial Companies [[6]](#ref6)
- **Federal Tax Authority (FTA)**: Accounting Standards Guide (CTGACS1) [[8]](#ref8)
- **Central Bank of the UAE (CBUAE)**: IFRS 9 and IFRS 17 Guidelines [[11]](#ref11)
- **ACCA Global**: UAECA Qualification [[10]](#ref10)
- **PwC Middle East**: UAE Corporate Tax Audited Financial Statements Update [[12]](#ref12)
- **Hawksford**: UAE Tax and Accounting Guide [[7]](#ref7)
- **IFRS Foundation**: IFRS 18 and Sustainability Standards [[13]](#ref13)

