('finance','03_Audit_Assurance_Ethics_and_Professional_Standards',null,'Certification exemption verification note','Some secondary sources in the research suggested that ICAI (India) and ICAP (Pakistan) holders may be exempt from IFRS/ISA exams for the AAA Fellowship; the source packet flags this as a conflict and indicates that primary AAA documentation should be checked before relying on any automatic exemption. Treat this as **[verify before reliance]** for candidates and employers.','finance 03 Audit Assurance Ethics and Professional Standards','03_Audit_Assurance_Ethics_and_Professional_Standards.md'),
('finance','04_Corporate_Finance_Valuation_MA_and_Restructuring',null,'1. Corporate Finance Scope','Corporate finance in the UAE covers capital allocation, investment appraisal, funding decisions, dividend policy, M&A, takeover rules for listed companies, restructuring reliefs, bankruptcy, valuation, and management performance analysis. The research base connects this chapter to the Commercial Companies Law, SCA/market rules, Corporate Tax, bankruptcy law, IFRS and valuation professional standards. [[1]](#ref1)[[1]](#ref1)','finance 04 Corporate Finance Valuation MA and Restructuring','04_Corporate_Finance_Valuation_MA_and_Restructuring.md'),
('finance','04_Corporate_Finance_Valuation_MA_and_Restructuring',null,'**Checklist Status (Path: `/data/workspace/.../RESEARCH_CHECKLIST.md`)**','*   **[Y]** Define domain scope and relevance to UAE finance library.
