---','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Structural design submission checklist','1. **Design basis memo** — State applicable code edition, risk category, load combinations, material specifications, exposure classes, and durability requirements.
2. **Geotechnical data** — Reference the approved soil investigation report; state assumed bearing capacity, pile type, pile depth and pile load test requirement.
3. **Load calculations** — Gravity loads (dead, superimposed dead, live), wind (ASCE 7 method with UAE wind maps), seismic (site class, spectral parameters), and any special loads (vibration, explosion, impact).
4. **Structural analysis** — Column/wall/slab/beam design with code check summaries, deflection and drift verification, and connection design for steel frames.
5. **Durability schedule** — Concrete cover, w/c ratio, cement type/GGBS/Fly Ash replacement, maximum chloride and sulfate content per exposure class.
6. **Foundation package** — Foundation type selection, bearing/pile capacity calculations, settlement analysis, factor of safety, and ITP for construction control.
7. **Drawing set review** — Check title block, revision cloud, dimensions, reinforcement bar marks, cover dimensions, splice details, connection details, embedded items, and coordination with MEP openings.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Site investigation and foundation construction checklist','1. **Borehole permit** — Obtain drilling permit from DM/DMT before mobilisation; confirm number, layout, and depth comply with Administrative Resolution 37/2021 requirements.
2. **Shoring design approval** — Submit shoring calculations and drawings; confirm maximum lateral displacement limit (40 mm for Trakhees) and minimum surcharge loads.
3. **Piling records** — Record pile ID, diameter, toe level, concrete volume, integrity test result, and static or dynamic load test as required.
4. **Dewatering permit** — Obtain permit for groundwater discharge; confirm discharge quality, route, and monitoring frequency with authority.
5. **Foundation inspection** — Authority inspection before concrete pour; confirm dimensions, reinforcement, cover, cleanliness, and any blinding concrete as required.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Template A: Design Review Checklist Framework','A senior engineering design review should confirm: design basis and load assumptions are documented; code edition and amendment dates are stated; all UAE authority requirements have been addressed by reference; specialist sub-consultant inputs are incorporated and coordinated; sustainability compliance (Al Sa''fat or Estidama as applicable) is addressed; fire and life safety interfaces are resolved; and the drawing set matches calculations and specifications. Any deviation from code requires a written technical justification.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Template B: Authority Submission Package','Before submitting to any UAE authority, confirm: the submitting consultant firm holds a valid practising card/approval for the project emirate; drawings are in the required format and coordinate system; all NOCs from upstream authorities are attached; calculations are signed by a registered engineer; the BIM model (if mandated under DM Circular 9-1-3/2026 or Abu Dhabi DMT requirements) is attached in the required format; and fees or bonds have been paid. Incomplete packages are returned without review in most Dubai and Abu Dhabi portals.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Template C: Site Supervision and Inspection Record','For each Witness or Hold point on the ITP, the site supervisor should confirm: the work activity matches the approved shop drawing; material has a valid test certificate or Material Approval Request (MAR); pre-activity conditions (compaction, formwork, earthing, cleanliness) are met; work execution matches approved method statement; post-activity tests are conducted and recorded; Non-Conformance Reports are raised immediately for failures; and the record is signed, dated, and uploaded to the document management system.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Template D: Commissioning and Handover Record','The commissioning package should include: signed Commissioning Manager appointment; pre-commissioning mechanical completion certificates; equipment startup records with measured versus specified values; functional test sheets for all systems; cause-and-effect matrix testing records for life-safety interfaces; Training records for the building operator; Operating and Maintenance manuals with as-built BIM model; and a Defect Tracking Register. In Dubai, DEWA/DCD and DM will conduct their own independent inspections before issuing the Completion Certificate.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Template E: Professional Risk Register for UAE Engineering Projects','Key project risks to track: BIM submission readiness; NOC expiry dates and renewal sequences; Specialist material lead times (high-performance concrete, specialist glazing, medical gas equipment); Third-party inspection availability; Civil Defense comments on fire systems; Authority variations discovered late in design; Structural peer review findings; Geotechnical report limitations; Weather restrictions on concrete pours; Power supply sequencing for DEWA connection; District Cooling provider connection timing; and Snagging management strategy for Completion Certificate.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Reinforced Concrete Design Parameters','Structural engineers in the UAE work primarily to ACI 318 (referenced by DBC 2021) or Eurocode 2 (EN 1992) depending on client preference and project type. Key practical parameters:

- **Characteristic concrete strength (f''c):** Typically C32/40 (fck=32 MPa) for suspended slabs and columns; C40/50 for transfer plates; C50/60 for high-rise cores and mat foundations.
- **Reinforcement yield strength (fy):** Grade 500 MPa (high ductility class B or C per BS 4449:2005) is the UAE industry standard. Grade 460 is still encountered in older projects.
- **Minimum slab thickness for deflection (ACI 318 Table 9.3.1.1):** Flat plate one-way: L/20; Two-way flat plate: L/30 (deflection-controlled spans).
- **Column axial load ratio:** Typically limited to 0.40–0.55 of Ag × f''c to maintain ductility in seismic design categories.
- **Coupling beam aspect ratio:** Diagonally reinforced coupling beams (preferred per ACI 318-19 Section 18.10.7) where ln/h < 2.0 in coupled shear wall systems.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Seismic Design in UAE Practice','The UAE is a low-to-moderate seismic region. Design parameters per DBC 2021 / ASCE 7-16 for Dubai:
- Risk Category II buildings: Ss ≈ 0.25g (0.2-second spectral acceleration), S1 ≈ 0.10g (1-second).
- Site Class D (stiff soil, Vs30 180–360 m/s) is common for coastal fill areas, requiring amplification factors.
- Seismic Design Category B or C is typical; Category D is triggered for specific occupancies or higher ground motions.
- Special Moment Frames (SMF) and Special Shear Walls are required for taller structures in SDC D.
- Site-specific probabilistic seismic hazard analysis (PSHA) is required for critical facilities, dams, and buildings over 73 m in Abu Dhabi.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Foundation Design Decision Matrix','| Site condition | Preferred foundation | Key design check |
|---|---|---|
| Dense sand/gravel, SPT N>30 | Raft or spread footings | Bearing capacity, differential settlement |
| Loose sand, SPT N<15 | Driven piles or ground improvement | Liquefaction potential, pile negative skin friction |
| Sabkha/salt flat | Replacement or deep piles bypassing sabkha | Expansion on wetting, sulfate-resistant cement |
| Rock (mudstone, limestone) | Bored piles or rock anchors | Rock socket bond, core recovery (RQD) |
| High water table, deep basement | Secant pile wall + slab, dewatering | Heave, flotation check, dewatering discharge permit |','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Pile Design and Testing Requirements','For bored cast-in-place piles in Dubai:
- **Preliminary pile test:** 1.5× working load, bi-directional (Osterberg cell) or top-down static test; minimum 1 per pile type per project.
- **Working pile test:** 1.0× working load; minimum 2% of total piles or 5 piles, whichever is greater.
- **Integrity testing:** Sonic integrity test (SIT) or cross-hole sonic logging (CSL) on 100% of piles >600 mm diameter.
- **Concrete cube test:** 3 cubes per 50 m³ poured; design strength typically C40–C50.
- **Shaft resistance:** Alpha-method for cohesive soils; beta-method or SPT-based correlations for sandy soils and rock sockets.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering',null,'Structural Steel Design','AISC 360 (LRFD method) is the primary reference for structural steel in DBC 2021. Eurocodes are accepted for specialty bridges and infrastructure.
- **Connection design:** All connections must be designed and detailed; AISC Prequalified Connections (AISC 358) are accepted for Special Moment Frames.
- **Corrosion protection:** ISO 12944 C5-M or C5-I system for coastal and marine exposure; minimum DFT (dry film thickness) per manufacturer''s coating system specification.
- **Fire protection:** Passive fire protection (intumescent paint, boarding, spray) sized for required fire resistance rating; steelwork in car parks with natural ventilation may qualify for unprotected in certain codes.
- **Welding:** All structural welds require Weld Procedure Specifications (WPS) and Procedure Qualification Records (PQR) per AWS D1.1; Trakhees specifically requires this by name.','procurement 01 Civil Structural and Geotechnical Engineering','01_Civil_Structural_and_Geotechnical_Engineering.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'1. Mechanical HVAC Engineering','# Source Packet 10: Mechanical HVAC engineering: ventilation, cooling loads, district cooling, ASHRAE, Dubai/Abu Dhabi requirements, equipment rooms and commissioning

**Research topic:** Mechanical HVAC engineering: ventilation, cooling loads, district cooling, ASHRAE, Dubai/Abu Dhabi requirements, equipment rooms and commissioning

**Report title:** Collector Report: Mechanical HVAC Engineering (UAE)

# Collector Report: Mechanical HVAC Engineering (UAE)

This report provides a comprehensive collection of source-backed engineering knowledge for Mechanical HVAC systems in the United Arab Emirates, focusing on regulatory compliance, technical design parameters, district cooling, and commissioning workflows.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'1. Executive Summary','The HVAC sector in the UAE is governed by stringent energy efficiency and safety regulations due to the extreme desert climate. Key developments in 2026 include the widespread adoption of the **Abu Dhabi Cooling Load Manual (CLM)** to combat system oversizing and the enforcement of the **Dubai Building Code (DBC) 2021**. District cooling remains the primary utility for high-density developments, regulated by the **RSB Dubai** to ensure high Delta T performance and sustainable water use.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'2. Coverage Table','| Dimension | Status | Evidence Source | Key Findings |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **Domain Scope** | Covered | Dubai Building Code (2021) | Focus on cooling, ventilation, and smoke control for high-rise and mixed-use. |
| **Authorities & Workflow** | Covered | DM, DMT, Trakhees, Civil Defense | Multi-stage approval: Concept -> Detailed Design -> NOC -> Inspection -> Completion. |
| **Codes & Standards** | Covered | DBC, ADIMC, UAE Fire Code, ASHRAE | DBC 2021, ADIMC 2013/2021, UAE Fire Code 2018, ASHRAE 62.1/90.1. |
| **Technical Design** | Covered | DM Health Facility Guidelines, AD CLM | Outdoor: 46°C DB / 29°C WB. Fresh Air: 34°C DB / 32°C WB. |
| **District Cooling** | Covered | RSB Dubai, South Energy Guidelines | Mandatory 9°C Delta T; 2-way valves only; ETS room technical specs. |
| **Ventilation & IAQ** | Covered | ASHRAE 62.1, Al Sa''fat | Minimum ventilation rates per occupancy; CO2 monitoring for high-density. |
| **Equipment Rooms** | Covered | DBC Part H, ADIMC | Clearances (min 1m), drainage (1 drain/144 sqft), and ventilation requirements. |
| **Commissioning** | Covered | DM Building Control, BSRIA/CIBSE | TAB (Testing, Adjusting, Balancing) is mandatory for completion certificates. |
| **Climate & Durability** | Covered | UAE Fire Code, Al Sa''fat | High humidity (latent load), dust filtration (MERV 13+), and corrosion protection. |','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'3.1 Outdoor and Indoor Design Conditions','Designers must adhere to emirate-specific weather data to prevent oversizing, a major focus of the 2026 Abu Dhabi Cooling Load Manual.
- **Dubai (DM Requirements):**
  - **Cooling Load Calculation:** 46°C Dry Bulb (DB), 29°C Wet Bulb (WB).
  - **Fresh Air Intake:** 34°C DB, 32°C WB.
  - *Source:* DHA Health Facility Guidelines (Mechanical HVAC), )%20Engineering%20Design [[3]](#ref3)
- **Abu Dhabi (CLM 2026):**
  - The **Abu Dhabi Cooling Load Manual (CLM)** aims to reduce AC oversizing by 25-35%, potentially saving AED 560 million annually in equipment costs.
  - *Source:* Abu Dhabi Media Office [[4]](#ref4)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'3.2 District Cooling & Energy Transfer Stations (ETS)','District cooling is mandatory in many Dubai/Abu Dhabi zones. The **Regulatory and Supervisory Bureau (RSB)** sets the technical standards.
- **Delta T Management:** A minimum Delta T (temperature difference between supply and return) of **9°C** is typically required. Failure to maintain this results in "Low Delta T" penalties.
- **Valve Requirements:** Three-way bypass valves are strictly prohibited; only **two-way modulating valves** are allowed to maintain high return temperatures.
- **ETS Room Specs:** Must include Plate Heat Exchangers (PHEX) with a 1°C approach temperature, energy meters, and dedicated BMS integration.
- *Source:* RSB Dubai Efficient Cooling, ; South Energy ETS Guidelines [[5]](#ref5)[[6]](#ref6)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'3.3 Ventilation and Smoke Control','- **IAQ Standards:** Systems must comply with **ASHRAE 62.1**. For high-occupancy areas, Demand Controlled Ventilation (DCV) using CO2 sensors is required by **Al Sa''fat** (Dubai Green Building System).
- **Smoke Management:** The **UAE Fire and Life Safety Code (2018)** mandates mechanical smoke extraction for atriums, corridors, and basements. Pressurization is required for fire stairs and lift shafts.
- *Source:* UAE Fire and Life Safety Code of Practice [[7]](#ref7)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'4.1 Dubai Municipality (DM) / Trakhees','1. **Concept Stage:** Submission of MEP concept report and sustainability (Al Sa''fat) strategy.
2. **Detailed Design:** Submission of cooling load calculations (HAP/Trace), ventilation schedules, and P&IDs.
3. **NOCs:** Required from DEWA (power/water) and District Cooling providers (Empower/Emicool).
4. **Execution:** Regular site inspections by DM Building Control.
5. **Completion:** Submission of TAB reports and O&M manuals for the Completion Certificate.
- *Source:* Dubai Municipality Building Permit Procedures [[8]](#ref8)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'4.2 Abu Dhabi (DMT / ADM)','- Projects must comply with the **Abu Dhabi International Mechanical Code (ADIMC)** and **Estidama Pearl Rating System**.
- **Estidama:** HVAC systems must meet minimum Energy Performance (RE-R1) and IAQ (IDP-R1) requirements.
- *Source:* Abu Dhabi DMT Building Permits [[9]](#ref9)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('legal','UAE_Environmental_Sustainability_and_Safety_Regulations',null,'15.1 Climate and Atmosphere','*   **UNFCCC & Paris Agreement**: UAE was the first in the region to sign and ratify. Committed to Net Zero 2050.
*   **Montreal Protocol**: Regulation of Ozone Depleting Substances (ODS). UAE has successfully phased out CFCs and is phasing out HCFCs.','legal UAE Environmental Sustainability and Safety Regulations','UAE_Environmental_Sustainability_and_Safety_Regulations.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'5.1 Equipment Room Requirements','- **Clearances:** Minimum 1000mm clearance around major equipment (Chillers, AHUs) for maintenance.
- **Drainage:** At least one sanitary floor drain for every **144 square feet** in equipment rooms.
- **Plinths:** Equipment must be mounted on concrete plinths at least 100mm-150mm high.
- *Source:* Dubai Building Code Part H; ADIMC Section 306.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'5.2 Commissioning (Cx) and TAB','- **TAB (Testing, Adjusting, and Balancing):** Mandatory for all air and water systems. Reports must be certified by an independent third-party agency.
- **Handover:** O&M manuals must include as-built drawings, equipment schedules, warranty certificates, and the final TAB report.
- *Source:* HVAC Testing & Commissioning Guide UAE [[10]](#ref10)','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'6.1 Design Review Checklist','- [ ] Verify outdoor design conditions match DM/ADM requirements (46°C DB).
- [ ] Ensure Sensible Heat Ratio (SHR) accounts for high latent loads in coastal areas.
- [ ] Confirm no 3-way valves are used in District Cooling circuits.
- [ ] Check that MERV 13 filters are specified for AHUs (Al Sa''fat/Estidama).
- [ ] Validate smoke damper locations against Fire & Life Safety drawings.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'6.2 Common Mistakes in UAE HVAC Design','- **Oversizing:** Using "rule of thumb" (e.g., 1 TR per 150 sqft) instead of detailed HAP calculations, leading to humidity issues and high energy bills.
- **Inadequate Latent Cooling:** Failing to account for extreme humidity (32°C WB) during fresh air treatment.
- **Poor ETS Design:** Low Delta T due to incorrect PHEX selection or bypasses.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'7. Gaps and Verification Notes','- **ADIMC 2021 Adoption:** While ADIMC 2013 is the widely cited base, verification is needed on the full enforcement of the 2021 version across all Abu Dhabi municipalities as of July 2026.
- **Refrigerant Phase-out:** Specific UAE-wide timelines for the phase-out of HFCs (like R-410A) in favor of low-GWP alternatives (R-32, R-454B) are evolving; check latest MOCCAE circulars.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('procurement','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM',null,'8. Checklist Status Summary','Checklist file: `/data/workspace/019f4636-87f2-76f3-9ef8-992dacac6848/research/e51031c0/RESEARCH_CHECKLIST.md`
- [Y] All items completed.','procurement 02 MEP HVAC Electrical Plumbing Fire and BIM','02_MEP_HVAC_Electrical_Plumbing_Fire_and_BIM.md'),
('legal','UAE_Environmental_Sustainability_and_Safety_Regulations',null,'21. NATIONAL ENVIRONMENTAL MONITORING NETWORK: STATIONS & PARAMETERS','The UAE maintains a sophisticated network of monitoring stations to provide real-time data on air, water, and soil quality.','legal UAE Environmental Sustainability and Safety Regulations','UAE_Environmental_Sustainability_and_Safety_Regulations.md'),
