('legal','Official_Resources_and_Links',null,'15. How to Use This Directory Professionally','This directory is designed as a navigation layer. It does not replace the live government portal. For any filing, application or regulated decision, use the portal listed here to obtain the current form, fee, submission route, Arabic legal text and authentication requirement. Many UAE services require UAE PASS login, an Emirates ID, a corporate account, a trade licence number, a tenancy contract, a site plan, a land number, an establishment card, a tax registration number or an authorised representative.','legal Official Resources and Links','Official_Resources_and_Links.md'),
('legal','Official_Resources_and_Links',null,'15.1 Common authentication and document requirements','| Requirement | Where commonly used | Notes |
|---|---|---|
| UAE PASS | Federal and emirate digital services, e-signature, document access | National digital identity and single sign-on. Confirm whether the service requires verified UAE PASS, face verification or Emirates ID scan. |
| Emirates ID | ICP, banks, telecoms, healthcare, tenancy, labour and most resident services | Required for most resident-facing services and KYC. |
| Trade licence | DET/DED, free zones, tax, bank account, utility commercial accounts | Must match activity, legal name and establishment card where applicable. |
| Establishment card / immigration file | Visa and employee sponsorship services | Issued through GDRFA/ICP or relevant free zone. |
| Tenancy contract | Ejari/Tawtheeq, utility connection, visa and school admission | Dubai uses Ejari; Abu Dhabi uses Tawtheeq; other emirates use local systems. |
| Tax Registration Number (TRN) | FTA VAT, excise and corporate tax services | Managed through FTA/EmaraTax. |
| Site plan / affection plan | Building permits, utility connections, Civil Defence and road NOCs | Issued by land/municipality authority; must match title/plot data. |
| No Objection Certificate (NOC) | Construction, utilities, roads, telecom, aviation height, fire safety | NOC sequence varies by emirate and project jurisdiction. |','legal Official Resources and Links','Official_Resources_and_Links.md'),
('legal','Official_Resources_and_Links',null,'15.2 Government service workflow patterns','Most UAE portals follow one of these patterns:

| Pattern | Steps | Examples |
|---|---|---|
| Individual resident service | UAE PASS login → Emirates ID verification → service form → upload documents → payment → digital certificate | Emirates ID renewal, visa status, police certificate, health card, tenancy registration. |
| Company licensing service | Create account → reserve trade name → initial approval → lease/office proof → activity approvals → payment → licence issue | DET/Dubai licensing, ADDED, free-zone company setup. |
| Construction permit service | Consultant login → land data → design documents → NOC routing → Civil Defence/utility approvals → permit issue → inspections → completion certificate | Dubai Municipality, DMT/TAMM, Trakhees, Sharjah Municipality. |
| Tax compliance service | EmaraTax login → registration → TRN issue → periodic filing → payment/refund → audit correspondence | VAT, excise, corporate tax. |
| Regulated-sector licensing | Pre-application meeting → fit-and-proper / technical dossier → regulator review → conditional approval → inspection → licence | DFSA/FSRA/VARA/CBUAE healthcare regulators and Civil Defence contractors. |
| Dispute service | Register case/claim → pay filing fee → upload contract/evidence → hearing/mediation → judgment/award → enforcement | Dubai Courts, ADJD, DIFC Courts, ADGM Courts, DIAC, ADCCAC. |','legal Official Resources and Links','Official_Resources_and_Links.md'),
('legal','Official_Resources_and_Links',null,'16. Federal Government Portals — Expanded Use Notes','| Authority / Portal | URL | Primary users | Key services | Practical notes |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| UAE Government Portal | https://u.ae | Residents, citizens, investors, professionals | Life-event guides, federal service links, strategy pages, legal and policy explainers | Use as a starting point, not as final legal text. Follow links to ministry/regulator portals for filing. |
| UAE PASS | https://uaepass.ae | All residents/citizens needing digital government access | Digital identity, single sign-on, electronic signature | Many services require a verified account; corporate users may still need separate authority accounts. |
| ICP | https://icp.gov.ae | Residents, PROs, employers, travellers | Emirates ID, entry permits, residence visas, citizenship, status checks | For Abu Dhabi and Northern Emirates residency, ICP is central; Dubai immigration also uses GDRFA/Amer. |
| Federal Tax Authority | https://tax.gov.ae | Businesses, tax agents, individuals in taxable contexts | VAT, excise tax, corporate tax, guides, public clarifications | Use EmaraTax for filings; keep records and check deadline calendars. |
| EmaraTax | https://eservices.tax.gov.ae | Tax registrants and agents | Registration, returns, payments, refunds, correspondence | Requires account access and often UAE PASS; supports VAT, excise and corporate tax. |
| Ministry of Justice | https://www.moj.gov.ae | Lawyers, litigants, notaries, researchers | Federal courts, notary, legal services, lawyer registration | Use with elaws for legal text. Court jurisdiction varies by emirate. |
