| Higher education | CAA / free-zone education regulators | Programme accreditation, institutional licensing and professional recognition. |','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
('legal','UAE_General_Information',null,'17.2 Higher-education landscape','The UAE higher-education market includes federal universities, emirate-backed institutions, private universities, branch campuses and free-zone education hubs. Key names include UAE University, Khalifa University, University of Sharjah, American University of Sharjah, American University in Dubai, New York University Abu Dhabi, Sorbonne University Abu Dhabi, Heriot-Watt University Dubai, Middlesex University Dubai, Rochester Institute of Technology Dubai and many others. Professional users should check CAA licensing and programme accreditation where a degree is to be used for visa, engineering registration, healthcare licensing, legal admission or academic employment.','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
('legal','UAE_General_Information',null,'18.1 Regulator map','| Jurisdiction | Regulator | Scope |
