| Dubai | Dubai Health Authority (DHA) | Healthcare facility and professional licensing, insurance framework, clinical standards. |
| Abu Dhabi | Department of Health Abu Dhabi (DoH) | Healthcare licensing, insurance, health data, hospital performance and Malaffi. |
| Northern Emirates | MOHAP | Facility and professional licensing outside emirate-specific authorities. |
| DHCC | Dubai Healthcare City Authority | Healthcare free-zone licensing and clinical governance. |','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
('legal','UAE_General_Information',null,'18.2 Major healthcare themes','The UAE healthcare system combines mandatory insurance, public hospitals, private clinics, medical tourism, digital health information exchanges and strict licensing. Disease-burden priorities include diabetes, obesity, cardiovascular disease, cancer screening, road injuries and lifestyle-related chronic disease. Hospitals and clinics must manage licensing, facility inspections, professional credentialing, medical-device approvals, pharmaceuticals, insurance claims and data-protection obligations.','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
('legal','UAE_General_Information',null,'19.1 Cultural forms','| Cultural element | Detail | Professional relevance |
