| National dress | Kandura, ghitra/agal, abaya, shayla; context-specific etiquette | Hospitality, protocol, HR and public-facing service design. |','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
('legal','UAE_General_Information',null,'19.2 Religion and law in public life','Islam is the official religion and Sharia is a principal source of legislation at the constitutional level. At the same time, the UAE hosts a large non-Muslim expatriate population with churches, temples and designated places of worship. Public holidays follow both Gregorian dates and the Islamic lunar calendar. Ramadan affects working hours, hospitality operations, event scheduling and retail footfall. Alcohol, pork and nightlife operate through licensing systems and vary by emirate and venue type.','legal UAE General Information','UAE_General_Information.md'),
